# Mounts (decision 0024 P5; docs/specs/walker.md §16.1; docs/specs/lua-plugin-api.md §15.5;
# docs/specs/scenario-feed.md §6.5, revision "P5 travel"): the feed owns who rides what in
# a scenario: the player mounts a normal mount, its durability changes, the player
# dismounts from the client (answered by the feed), then mounts a war-steed whose morale,
# power and fury change, and another rider's mount is shown. Literal refs need no install;
# with one, the selectors give a normal mount effect and a war-steed effect of the install
# (their steps name selector elements, so without an install they are skipped).
tessera-scenario 1
title "Paddock"
tick 100ms
player "Tamsin"
select $horses = effect role=mount war-steed=no n=1 seed=4
select $steeds = effect role=mount war-steed=yes n=1 seed=6
actor $rider kind=player name="Rook" pos=4,0,0 facing=270

at 0s spawn $rider
+0.5s mount player "Grey pony" kind=basic
+0s mount player $horses[0]
+0s mount-vital player durability 90/100
+0.5s mount-vital player durability 75/100
+0.5s mount $rider "Bay horse"
on dismount
+0s mount player none
end
at 4s mount player "Dun steed" kind=combat
+0s mount player $steeds[0]
+0s mount-vital player morale 800/1000
+0s mount-vital player power 200/400
+0.5s mount-vital player fury 3/5
+0.5s mount-vital player morale 650/1000
+1s mount player none

input
at 2.5s dismount
end
